      "message": "PS 10 actually introduced a new bug. The vertex shader had been using the `maskBounds.LT` to convert the `maskCoords` variable (that was defined in the logical mask space) into the final atlas coordinate space. The maskBounds were already in the atlas coordinate space. Applying any inset or outset of 1/2px then shifted all of the texture sampling.\n\nBecause the texture coordinates and bounds have also already been normalized, it\u0027s tricky to just apply the inset/outset in the vertex shader after its used the top-left corner. I also didn\u0027t want to add an additional attribute to convey the texture origin.\n\nTo fix this, I adjusted how the maskToDevice matrix is decomposed. Previously it was post-applying the device origin translation. Now it calculates a translation that can be pre-applied. While this math is more complex, it means that the texture origin can be incorporated into the `deviceOrigin` instance attribute and both `drawBounds` and `maskBounds` are now uploaded in the same atlas coordinate space.\n\nThe new diff is PS9 to PS11.",
